17592186179454 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote the first number by $n$ and the second number by $k$, we can write \"the product of three and another number\" as $3k$.\n\nSo, the phrase \"a number minus the product of three and another number\" can be written as\n$n - 3k$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179455 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13063" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179455 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the phrase \"the quotient of a number and seven\" into an algebraic expression." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179455 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ce7fd393-cd41-5060-9ffe-422f6474102d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179455 #edb/ref 1074 "\"The quotient of a number and seven\" means the same thing as \"a number divided by seven.\" If we call our number $x$, then we can express this mathematically as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{7}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179815 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179815 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179815 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180224 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179815 #edb/ref 1039 "Translating Between Phrases and Algebraic Expressions Containing Multiplication" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179815 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179815 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "638adb60-4629-514c-86e9-fa824295dc43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179816 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179816 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179816 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179816 #edb/ref 1039 "Translating Between Phrases and Algebraic Expressions Containing Division" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179816 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179816 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "66bfa36e-be32-5c64-86c1-b17e8e670e04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179872 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186